;
; How Halloo files one call in its history, in MYRA (halloo_rules.h HR5):
; its number, the other node's member id, which way it went (0 in, 1 out),
; its media (0 audio, 1 audio and video), how it ended (zxvd's end_reason,
; 0 none to 10 cancelled), how long it was connected in ms, and when it
; ended in ms since 1970. The rules say what the values may mean; this
; says whether they make a record.
^ZXHALLOO(seq:i9) = peer:i10! ^ dir:i1! ^ media:i1! ^ reason:i2! ^ ms:i10! ^ stamp:i13!
